# Line endings are part of what these files mean.
#
# Git for Windows checks text files out with CRLF by default. One data file in
# this repo is parsed line by line, and a stray carriage return on the last word
# of each line silently broke every homophone group on a Windows checkout — the
# only platform this app is for. Source stays LF everywhere; Windows-only
# scripts would be the one place to opt in to CRLF, and there are none.
* text=auto eol=lf
src/data/homophones.txt text eol=lf
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.wav binary
